 his college classmates like both. So, this is impossible. Therefore, D cannot be true..\n\nWait, let me make sure I'm not making a mistake here. The context says none of his college classmates like both rock climbing and shooting. So, if D says half of them like both, that directly contradicts the given information. Therefore, D cannot be true..\n\nSo, putting it all together:.\n\nA: Possible, because John could like swimming..\n\nB: True, as all classmates like swimming..\n\nC: Possible, as middle school classmates aren't restricted from liking both..\n\nD: Impossible, as it contradicts the given information. Therefore, the option is "]] 10%|9         | 59/600 [01:13<10:23,  1.15s/it]
