formance. It's more about feasibility rather than the validity of his claim..\n\nOption B: Profits from SSDs are higher than traditional drives. This seems unrelated. It's about business profits, not about performance or the reason behind slow laptops. So probably not the answer..\n\nOption C: Some old laptops have poor CPU and memory. Wait, Mr. Tian said that the main issue isn't CPU or memory, but the hard disk. If some laptops do have poor CPU or memory, does that challenge his view? Well, if a small number have those issues, it doesn't contradict his main point that the majority's problem is the hard disk. So maybe not the strongest counter..\n\nOption D: Gaming experience depends a lot on the graphics card, which is poor in old laptops. Oh, this is interesting. Mr. Tian attributes slow performance to the hard disk, but if the graphics card is the main issue, then even with an SSD, the gaming experience might not improve much. This directly challenges his assumption that the hard disk is the main culprit. Therefore, the option is "]]
