e..\n\nSo, the key points here are:.\n1. Lexicographers don't change vocabulary randomly; they research carefully..\n2. They can't ignore a basic fact: languages are used by the masses and have a broad social nature..\n3. Therefore, standardization must follow the mass line, meaning it should serve the masses..\n\nLooking at the options:.\nA) Lexicographers can't change vocabulary at will. This is mentioned, but it's more about their approach rather than the basic requirement..\nB) They should know the lexicography process. Not directly mentioned in the passage..\nC) Standardization must serve the broad masses. This aligns with the idea that it follows the mass line..\nD) The masses decide standardization. The passage says it must follow the mass line, but doesn't say the masses decide it directly. Therefore, the option is "]]
