an strengthen it. Therefore, this option is probably not the correct answer..\n\nOption D: The device gives a distinctive reading when the signals it detects come from human beings rather than from any other living beings. This is interesting because it means the device can differentiate between human signals and those from other animals or sources. This specificity would be crucial in a rescue scenario. If the device can accurately identify human signals, it reduces the chances of false positives or distractions, making it more reliable for emergency teams. This directly supports the argument by showing that the device is not only effective at detecting signals but also at distinguishing the relevant ones, which would make it more useful in real-world applications. Therefore, the option is "]] 77%|#######7  | 464/600 [20:01<02:46,  1.23s/it]
