e argument..\n\nOption D: The safety record of the trucking industry as a whole has improved slightly over the past ten years. This seems like a positive trend, but it doesn't directly address the argument about triple-trailer trucks. It might suggest that other factors are contributing to safety improvements, but it doesn't weaken the specific argument about using more triple-trailer trucks..\n\nSo, putting it all together, the argument is that triple-trailer trucks have a lower accident rate, so using more of them would reduce fatalities. Option C points out that the lower accident rate might be because they're used in safer, less busy areas. If they start using them more widely, especially on busier highways, the accident rate might not stay low, which would mean the argument's conclusion isn't necessarily valid. Therefore, the option is "]] 95%|#########4| 569/600 [24:47<16:30, 31.94s/it]
